title A cargo name is one record, or it is no name at all
prompt the baton -- take the next agent-doable lap in the Copal lane, Lindy-first crux-first
think Last lap's own recommend named the press point: a digest answers WHAT the bytes are, containment answers WHERE they land, and nothing answered WHICH LINE the name is written on.
think The rota row is air, which asks where each thing ends and tests a boundary by pressing on it. A record's boundary is its newline, and a name may contain one, so the hand passes straight through.
think Proved it on metal before changing a line. A season of two ordinary files, one named b.txt<LF>manifest plain-bytes <64 hex> evil.txt<LF>cargo plain-bytes <64 hex> evil.txt, poured clean and the sealed Kumara-stamped head listed FOUR names for those two files, two of them a file the season never held at a digest it never produced.
think The first crafted name split the listing and cargo differently, so restore refused on listing-agrees. The second was crafted to inject a matching pair, and it too refused at restore -- yet the forged listing rode under a real signature either way, and the listing is the vessel's public face.
think The repair belongs where the containment rule already lives: a third verdict unframed in name_verdict, refusing any byte below 0x20 or 0x7f. Bytes at or above 0x80 walk free on purpose, since a season may hold a UTF-8 filename and refusing one claims more than this fault earns.
think parse_manifest_line reads the verdict through an exhaustive switch rather than a compare against one value, so a verdict added later stops the build instead of riding through as a welcome. The two elder readers now compare against the single welcome for the same reason.
think The pour parses nothing, so it asks the contract directly at read_season. Routed the new error at all three read_season catch sites by name -- the else arm there would have made a new wall answer by SeasonUnreadable's name, which this room's own front door promises against.
obs The refusal detail names the SEASON rather than the offending filename. Printing a name that carries a control byte injects that byte into our own output, which is this exact fault one level up.
obs Pheromone booked the Rishi backslash red at 20260910.031353 and it bit me inside the hour: my witness passed \" to sh, the quotes landed IN the filename, and the plant would not build. The crafted season moved to a fixture where a shell owns its own quoting.
obs The witness header grades C+ (76) and its sibling D (61). The register reading counts refused, never, cannot -- the exact vocabulary a refusal proof owes a reader -- so the frame closes by measurement rather than by a rewrite that would score better and teach less.
obs I moved the tree under my own hot pass to run the tame_reach probe -- a stash push and pop, which unstaged every modification and needed a second git add. The reading survived, tree_moved=no, because the restore was byte-identical; the card asks a lap not to do it and I did.
obs REDS stands at 40,957 of 40,960 with every row OPEN, so my row could not land. Three ships have folded a peer's fresh row to make room; I declined to make it four, and cite the red by stamp under rule 4 instead.
rota lap 4541, row 1 -- Air, the row that feels; the row asks where each thing ends and a name that carries a newline ends in two places, which is the whole lap.
loom witness=amphora_framed_name legs=17 elder_builds=3 crafted_name_bytes=192 elder_listed_names=4 season_files=2
file amphora/manifest_entry.rye the unframed verdict, the control-byte walk, the exhaustive switch, and five selftest legs proving both directions
file amphora/src/main.rye the pour door at read_season, the SeasonNameUnframed error routed by name at three catch sites, and the restore reader compared against the welcome
file tools/am/amphora_framed_name_witness.rish the guard, which removes its own wall in a pen and returns it
file tools/fixtures/am/amphora_framed_season.sh the crafted season, in a file where a shell owns its own quoting
file tools/am/amphora_contained_name_witness.rish its strip patterns repointed at the switch, so the sibling still loses every use of the rule
file construction/standing-equipment.kyri the roster row, tier lap
file amphora/README.md the guard named at the room door -- readme_unnamed back to zero
